 "text": "Hey, good to have you along. How are you? The best way is usually as separate container in the fridge, then reusing it as a cooler on Sunday. If you have to keep it in the car, keep it as dry as possible. blocks are good, but only if they keep them flat. If they stack, the cold stays in the bottom one and the top ones warm up fast. A dry bag is useful if it rains or you leave it in the trunk overnight. Fill it with dry clothes before you put in the cooler, so it doesn't compress. Keep a tight seal with tape and clips, and only open it when you ready to use it. A cold cooler lasts longer. Fill it up before you start the weekend, and only use what you've used up. If you leave it running, it can warm up.",
